  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1218 PM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nTemperatures have rebounded nicely thus far today after this\nmorning's rather chilly lows down into the 30s area-wide under\nextensive 1030mb high pressure from western Ontario province\nsouth to the Missouri River Valley. This has allowed for mostly\nsunny skies and temperatures rising into the lower 60s to lower\n70s. Warm air advection will continue tonight as a warm front\napproaches from the Dakotas and will cross MN/WI overnight.\nDespite plenty of low level dry air in place, enough forcing\nwith meager moisture convergence ahead of the warm front may be\nenough to squeeze out a few rain showers over central MN into\nnorthwest WI this evening.\n\nTemperatures will surge to well-above normal levels on Tuesday\nwith highs a couple/few degrees either side of 80 throughout the\nWFO MPX coverage area. Breezy/gusty conditions are also expected\nas strong LLJ aloft overnight will blend down to the surface due\nto deep mixing profiles expected tomorrow. The associated cold\nfront will move across the region late Tuesday afternoon through\nTuesday evening, bringing an end to the late summer-like\nconditions and allowing more seasonable temperatures to return\nfor the remainder of the week. Highs will remain in the mid 60s\nto lower 70s throughout the week, outside of a small bump on\nSaturday as another warm sector moves through the region,\nfollowed by another cold front for Sunday.\n\nAfter this evening, no precipitation is expected across the\ncoverage area until possibly late Sunday into Monday with the\nweekend cold front.",
